E = \frac{(6.6 \times 10^{-34} \text{ Js})(3 \times 10^8 \text{ ms}^{-1})}{5 \times 10^{-7} \text{ m}}= 3.96 \times 10^{-19} \text{ J}
\Rightarrow 3.96 \times 10^{-19} = 2.3 \times 1.6 \times 10^{-19} + \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{max}}^{2}= 3.68 \times 10^{-19} + \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{max}}^{2}
v_{\text{max}}^2 = \frac{2 \times 0.28 \times 10^{-19}}{m} = \frac{2 \times 0.28 \times 10^{-19}}{9.1 \times 10^{-31}}
v_{\text{max}} = \sqrt{\frac{0.56 \times 10^{-19} \,\text{J}}{9.1 \times 10^{-31} \,\text{kg}}} = 2.5 \times 10^5 \,\text{m s}^{-1}
(iii) The stopping potential V_0 is given as
eV_0 = \frac{1}{2}mv_{\text{max}}^2
V_0 = \frac{0.28 \times 10^{-19} \,\text{J}}{1.6 \times 10^{-19} \,\text{JV}^{-1}} = 0.18 \,\text{V}
